  "reason": "RNA-only scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool is currently the strongest result (acc 0.650, F1 0.628), while the only multimodal test so far (config_030, same RNA encoder/aggregation but resnet50 concat) is slightly lower (acc 0.632, F1 0.607) and image-only resnet50 is weak. This leaves uncertainty about whether the multimodal shortfall is due to the weak image encoder rather than fusion or the multimodal setup itself. config_036 tests that by replacing resnet50 with imagenet_vit_l while holding RNA encoder, profile setting, aggregation, and concat fusion fixed relative to config_030. If it improves, image representation is a key lever and multimodal ViT-L is worth exploiting; if not, image fusion with this RNA setup is less promising. It is a single-change, high-information extension of the best RNA direction and has stronger potential to approach or beat the current best than image-only or fusion-only checks."
